WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.191
Idea. A cinema has two seats in row one, seven in row two, twelve in row three. Every row has five more. How many seats are in the first n rows? Adding them all up is a sum.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:26.352
Sigma means add up. Sigma from r equals one to n of five r minus three says: put r equal to one, two, three, up to n, and add. That gives two plus seven plus twelve, and so on.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:39.953
A rule like five r minus three always gives an arithmetic series. The first term a is the value at r equals one. The common difference d is the number in front of r. There are n terms.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:50.917
Then use the sum formula. The sum of n terms, called S n, is n over two, times, two a plus n minus one times d. You must know this formula.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:59.319
These questions say show that. The sum is printed, so every line must be written. You end exactly at the printed result.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:09.420
Method. Step one: put r equal to one, two, three to see the first terms. Step two: state a and d, and say there are n terms.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:18.971
Step three: put a, d and n into the sum formula. Step four: simplify inside the bracket, line by line, to the printed answer.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:25.287
The trap is the first term. Here the number added is minus three, but the first term is two.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:39.365
Worked example. June twenty twenty four, paper one. Show that the sum from r equals one to n of five r minus three equals n over two, times five n minus one. Three marks.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.788
Step one: put r equal to one, two, three. We get two, seven and twelve.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:53.785
The jump is five, so the series is arithmetic. The first term a is two, the common difference d is five, and there are n terms.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:02:02.408
Step three: write the formula and substitute. N over two, times, two times two, plus n minus one times five.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:09.753
Step four: simplify inside the bracket. Four plus five n minus five is five n minus one.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:20.538
Reject a tempting route. Taking the first term as minus three gives n over two, times five n minus eleven. That does not match the printed answer.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:42.224
Check with n equal to four. Two plus seven plus twelve plus seventeen is thirty eight. The formula gives four over two times nineteen, also thirty eight. The sum equals n over two, times five n minus one, as required. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:55.723
Common mistake. Another mistake is the last term. If you use the sum of first plus last, the last term is the value at r equals n, which is five n minus three. Not five n.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:11.885
Your turn. Now you try, from June twenty twenty three. Show that the sum from r equals one to n of three r plus two equals n over two, times three n plus seven. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:21.076
Answer. Put r equal to one, two, three. We get five, eight, eleven. So a is five and d is three, with n terms.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:31.790
Substitute into the formula. N over two, times ten plus three n minus three. That simplifies to n over two, times three n plus seven.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:40.860
The common wrong answer takes the first term as two. That gives n over two times three n plus one. It is not the printed result.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:47.274
Remember the method. Write the terms, state a, d and n, substitute, and simplify.
